U3: Which expression is equivalent to 9(5t+3)+3t",Start with \(9(5t+3)+3t\). First multiply the 9 into the parentheses: \[ 9(5t+3)=9\cdot 5t + 9\cdot 3 = 45t + 27 \] Now add the \(+3t\): \[ 45t+27+3t = 48t+27 \] So an equivalent expression is **\(48t+27\)**.,Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1754,64,0.000804,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
