U3: Factor the sum or difference of two cubes: 27t^3 + 125.","**\(27t^3 + 125\) is a sum of cubes:** \((3t)^3 + 5^3\). Use \(a^3+b^3=(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2)\) with \(a=3t,\; b=5\): \[ 27t^3+125=(3t+5)\big((3t)^2-(3t)(5)+5^2\big) =(3t+5)(9t^2-15t+25). \] **Final:** \(\mathbf{(3t+5)(9t^2-15t+25)}\).",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1796,64,0.000821,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
