U7: But what is power of 3","**“Power of 3” usually means \(3\) raised to some exponent.** For example, \(3^2\) is read “3 to the power 2.” - \(3^1 = 3\) - \(3^2 = 3 \times 3 = 9\) - \(3^3 = 3 \times 3 \times 3 = 27\) So “powers of 3” are numbers like **3, 9, 27, 81, …** (each time you multiply by 3).",Lesson_request,,,,,Academic,,,,1804,62,0.000821,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
