U18: Question no. 16 Question 16 asks to verify the trigonometric identity involving cos A, tan A, sin² A, and (cos A − sin A), shown in a textbook image.","**Question 16: Prove that** \[ \frac{\cos A}{1-\tan A}-\frac{\sin^2 A}{\cos A-\sin A} =\cos A+\sin A \] Using \(\tan A=\dfrac{\sin A}{\cos A}\), \[ 1-\tan A =1-\frac{\sin A}{\cos A} =\frac{\cos A-\sin A}{\cos A} \] Therefore, \[ \frac{\cos A}{1-\tan A} =\frac{\cos A}{\frac{\cos A-\sin A}{\cos A}} =\",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2326,64,0.001033,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
