U14: B. A stadium has 45 seats in one row. What is the seating capacity of the station if there are 2,340 kows?","**Multiply seats per row by number of rows.** There are \(45\) seats in one row and \(2{,}340\) rows (I’m assuming “kows” means **rows**), so: \[ 45 \times 2{,}340 \] Break \(45\) into \(40+5\): \[ 2{,}340 \times 40 = 93{,}600 \] \[ 2{,}340 \times 5 = 11{,}700 \] Add: \[ 93{,}600 + 11{,}700 = 105{,}",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2313,64,0.001028,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
8ee0da8c-ca3b-43fa-bd32-a8047619c6d8,2026-08-17T14:08:51.200Z,1,3,"U1: 30 + (16-f/2-f)
