U3: 3q Question 3 asks the student to simplify the expression negative one-fourth plus five-twelfths.",For question **3**: \[ \left(-\frac14\right)+\left(\frac{5}{12}\right) \] The LCM of \(4\) and \(12\) is \(12\). Convert \(-\frac14\) to twelfths: \[ -\frac14=-\frac{3}{12} \] Now add: \[ -\frac{3}{12}+\frac{5}{12} =\frac{2}{12} =\boxed{\frac16} \] **Answer: \(\frac{1}{6}\)**,Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1846,64,0.000841,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
