U17: Find the LCM and HCF of the following numbers in which one number is the factors of the other number 6,48 and 12,84 and 19,95 and 24,216","**When one number is a factor of the other:** - **HCF = the smaller number** - **LCM = the bigger number** So: - For \(6, 48\): **HCF = 6**, **LCM = 48** - For \(12, 84\): **HCF = 12**, **LCM = 84** - For \(19, 95\): **HCF = 19**, **LCM = 95** - For \(24, 216\): **HCF = 24**, **LCM = 216**",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1933,64,0.000876,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
