U3: 3(2x − 8) – 11x. What are algebraic expressions that are equivalent to this expression",Expand and combine like terms: \[ 3(2x-8)-11x = (3\cdot 2x) + (3\cdot -8) - 11x = 6x - 24 - 11x \] Now combine the \(x\)-terms: \[ 6x-11x = -5x \] So an equivalent expression is: \[ \boxed{-5x - 24} \] Other equivalent forms include \(\boxed{-(5x+24)}\) or \(\boxed{-24-5x}\).,Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1863,64,0.000848,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
