U5: What formulae u used","**I didn’t use a special “formula” here—I used the distributive property (FOIL), which means multiply each term in one bracket by each term in the other.** For \((a+2)(a-1)\), the idea is: \[ (x+y)(m+n)=xm+xn+ym+yn \] So: \[ (a+2)(a-1)=a\cdot a+a\cdot(-1)+2\cdot a+2\cdot(-1) \] \[ = a^2-a+2a-2 = \ma",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1843,64,0.000840,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
