U3: How many perfect squares are there in between 1 to 90","**The perfect squares between 1 and 90 are \(1^2,2^2,3^2,\dots\) up to the largest square \(\le 90\).** \(9^2 = 81 \le 90\) but \(10^2 = 100 > 90\), so the squares are \(1^2\) through \(9^2\). That’s **9 perfect squares**: \(1,4,9,16,25,36,49,64,81\).",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1800,64,0.000822,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
