**Q1) Use Euclid’s division algorithm to find the HCF of \(867\) and \(255\).** 
I’m keeping extra digits exact (no rounding needed here).

\[
867 = 255 \times 3 + 102
\]
\[
255 = 102 \times 2 + 51
\]
\[
102 = 51 \times 2 + 0
\]

When the remainder becomes \(0\), the last non-zero remainder is the HCF.

So the HCF is **\(\mathbf{51}\)**.

