U12: In simple","**A matrix is just a rectangular table of numbers** written in brackets, like 
\[
A=\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\3&4\end{bmatrix}
\]
It has **rows** (horizontal) and **columns** (vertical). The **order** (size) is written as \(m\times n\) = (rows \(\times\) columns), so this one is \(2\times2\).

**Basic operations (simple):**
- **Add/Subtract:** only if same order. Add matching positions. 
\[
\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\3&4\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}5&6\\7&8\end{bmatrix}
=\begin{bmatrix}6&8\\10&12\end{bmatrix}
\]
- **Multiply by a number (scalar):** multiply every entry. 
\[
3\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\3&4\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}3&6\\9&12\end{bmatrix}
\]
- **Multiply two matrices:** you can do \(AB\) only if **columns of \(A\) = rows of \(B\)**. Each entry is “row × column” dot product. 
\[
\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\3&4\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}5&6\\7&8\end{bmatrix}
=\begin{bmatrix}(1\cdot5+2\cdot7)&(1\cdot6+2\cdot8)\\(3\cdot5+4\cdot7)&(3\cdot6+4\cdot8)\end{bmatrix}
=\begin{bmatrix}19&22\\43&50\end{bmatrix}
\]

**What do you want next: (1) types of matrices, (2) determinant & inverse (2×2), or (3) solving equations using matrices?**",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic,,,0.9500,14267,215,0.003437,"The bot correctly and comprehensively answered the user's questions about half-life and reaction orders without any technical or contextual failures. The user shifted topic abruptly at the end without indicating frustration or dissatisfaction, so user sentiment is neutral. There are no detected bot failures or session pattern issues.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
