SECTION - A
Questions 1 to 10 earry 1 mark each.
1. Which expression always represents a multiple of 9?
(a) 9n
(b) \( 6 n+3 \)
(c) \( 3 n \)
(d) \( 9 n+1 \)
2. A number is written as \( 5 k+2 \). What remainder will it leave when divided by 5?
(a) 0
(b) 1
(c) 2
(d) 5
3. If a number is divisible by both 4 and 6, then it must be divisible by
(a) 8
(b) 12
(c) 18
(d) 24
