U6: I have not started yet I am in class 11th....e","**No problem—starting from zero is totally workable if you build the base the right way.** We’ll begin with **Mole Concept**, because it supports almost every chapter in Physical Chemistry.

I’ll teach one core idea, then you’ll do a few questions.

### 1) The one idea to learn first
**Moles = mass ÷ molar mass**

Example: water \(H_2O\) has molar mass \(18\,\text{g/mol}\) (because \(2\times1 + 16 = 18\)). 
So \(18\,\text{g}\) of water is:
\[
\text{moles} = \frac{18}{18} = 1 \text{ mol}
\]

### 2) Particles link (very important)
**Number of particles = moles × \(N_A\)**, where \(N_A = 6.022\times10^{23}\)

So \(0.50\) mol has:
\[
0.50 \times 6.022\times10^{23} = 3.011\times10^{23}\ \text{particles}
\]

### Now you try (do these 3)
Keep answers simple—no need to overthink.

**Q1.** Moles in \(9\,\text{g}\) of water \((H_2O,\ 18\,\text{g/mol})\)? 
**Q2.** Mass of \(2\) mol of \(\text{CO}_2\) \((M=44\,\text{g/mol})\)? 
**Q3.** Number of molecules in \(0.25\) mol of \(\text{O}_2\)? \(\;N_A = 6.022\times10^{23}\)

Reply: **1) … 2) … 3) …** 
Then I’ll check and move to **limiting reagent** (the next big skill).",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Mock / Practice Questions | Specific Named Resource | Slotfill,,,0.9800,14177,325,0.003501,The conversation is a coherent academic session focused on JEE Main exam preparation with appropriate practice questions and structured guidance. The bot uses slotfill templates correctly aligned with the user's academic intent and class level. There are no detected failures or mismatches in context or content.,0,full_rate,Academic,Study Plan / Syllabus,gate_llm,gate_llm
