U4: 11.12.13.14.15.16","**I can see you have a lot of questions here. I’ll explain how to do the first one (Q11).** 
Then you try Q12 and send your attempt (even 2–3 lines), and I’ll help you fix it.

**Q11 (mass \(10\,\text{kg}\), velocity–time graph Fig 6.41): find force using the graph**

1) From the velocity–time graph, read two clear points. The line starts at about 
\((t=0\,\text{s},\, v=10\,\text{m/s})\) and ends at about \((t=8\,\text{s},\, v=30\,\text{m/s})\).

2) Acceleration is the slope of the \(v\)-\(t\) graph:
\[
a=\frac{\Delta v}{\Delta t}=\frac{30-10}{8-0}=\frac{20}{8}=2.5\,\text{m/s}^2
\]

3) Force:
\[
F=ma=10\times 2.5=25\,\text{N}
\]

So the force acting on the object is **\(\mathbf{25\,N}\)** (in the direction of motion).

Now choose what you want next: **Q12 or Q13**? (Those don’t need the graph.)",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Specific Named Resource | Direct Response | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13636,278,0.003366,"The bot correctly answered and explained the user's academic questions with no factual or procedural errors. The user requested direct explanations rather than templates, which the bot accommodated without failure. There are no detected bot failures or session issues.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
