U5: every new year aunty be gives dollar 300 in the ratio of their ages this year the nases are aged 3 and 7 show that in 5 years time the younger get 32 more than she got this year Tom and the mean share dollar e in the ratio C is to D use algebra to write an expression for the amount that car will get the mean will get tombise to bags of chips for Dollar 2.40 workeout the cost of one bag of chips v 5 bags of chips","**I can see you have a lot of questions here. I’ll explain how to do the first one.**

Aunty gives \(\$300\) shared in the ratio of their ages.

This year, ages are \(3\) and \(7\), so the ratio is \(3:7\). 
Total parts \(= 3+7 = 10\).

Younger’s share this year:
\[
300 \times \frac{3}{10} = 90
\]

In 5 years, ages will be \(8\) and \(12\), so the ratio is \(8:12\). 
Total parts \(= 8+12 = 20\).

Younger’s share in 5 years:
\[
300 \times \frac{8}{20} = 120
\]

Difference:
\[
120 - 90 = 30
\]

So in 5 years, the younger gets **\(\$30\)** more than this year (not \(\$32\)).

