U5: Both","**I can explain both, but I need the figures to write the *exact* journal entries.** Without numbers, I can show the *standard entries* you use in Grade 12 accounting.

### **1) Under-subscription (applications shares offered)**
Some applicants don’t get shares (or get fewer). Extra application money is handled by **refund** and/or **adjustment toward allotment/calls**.

**(a) On receipt of application money**
\[
\text{Bank A/c Dr} \\
\quad \text{To Share Application A/c}
\]

**(b) If excess application money is refunded**
\[
\text{Share Application A/c Dr} \\
\quad \text{To Bank A/c}
\]

**(c) Transfer application money for shares allotted**
\[
\text{Share Application A/c Dr} \\
\quad \text{To Share Capital A/c}
\]

**(d) If excess application money is adjusted against allotment (instead of refund)**
\[
\text{Share Application A/c Dr} \\
\quad \text{To Share Allotment A/c}
\]

Then normal allotment and call entries:
\[
\text{Share Allotment A/c Dr \quad To Share Capital A/c}
\]
\[
\text{Bank A/c Dr \quad To Share Allotment A/c}
\]

---

