Given: four-pole, \(200\ \text{V}\) **lap wound** generator, \(Z=400\) conductors, speed \(N=300\ \text{rpm}\). 
For a DC generator,
\[
E = \frac{P\Phi Z N}{60A}
\]
For **lap winding**, \(A=P\). So it simplifies to
\[
E=\frac{\Phi Z N}{60}
\]

Substitute:
\[
200=\frac{\Phi(400)(300)}{60}
\]
Compute \(\frac{400\cdot 300}{60}=400\cdot 5=2000\):
\[
200 = 2000\Phi \Rightarrow \Phi = \frac{200}{2000}=0.1\ \text{Wb}
\]

**Useful flux per pole: \(\mathbf{\Phi = 0.10\ \text{Wb/pole}}\).**

