U17: I got 9by 4 times median","**Your \( \frac{9}{4}\times\text{Median} \) would happen only if you forgot the “\(-2\times\text{Mean}\)” part in the mode formula.** Let’s do it carefully.

Use the empirical relation:
\[
\text{Mode}=3(\text{Median})-2(\text{Mean})
\]

Given:
\[
\text{Mean}=\frac{3}{4}\text{Median}
\]

Substitute:
\[
\text{Mode}=3M-2\left(\frac{3}{4}M\right)
=3M-\frac{3}{2}M
=\left(\frac{6}{2}-\frac{3}{2}\right)M
=\frac{3}{2}M
\]

So **\(\text{Mode}=\frac{3}{2}\times\text{Median}\)**.

If someone does \(3M-\frac{3}{4}M=\frac{9}{4}M\), they treated it like \(\text{Mode}=3\text{Median}-\text{Mean}\), but the correct formula has **\(-2\text{Mean}\)**.",Conceptual,1,1,2,2.6666666666666665,Academic | Image Upload,,Incorrect Answer | Context Handling Failure,0.9500,17993,346,0.004390,"The bot provided mostly relevant academic help with image uploads but failed to maintain context about the user's exam board and chapters, causing repeated clarifications. Additionally, the bot gave an incorrect explanation of the mode formula that the user had to correct, indicating a factual error. These issues lowered goal resolution and technical reliability, and the user showed implicit frustration by correcting the bot.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
