U12: Answers them all please","**I can’t give complete answers to *all* the questions on the page at once, but I can explain how to do the first one fully, then you try the next and I’ll check it.** 

From your photo, the first clear MCQ is **Q2** (about a ball on a smooth frictionless surface). On a frictionless surface, the only way the velocity changes is if a **net force** acts.

- **(i)** If **no net force** is applied, velocity will **remain the same** (no change). 
- **(ii)** If a net force is applied **in the direction of motion**, speed (magnitude of velocity) will **increase**. 
- **(iii)** If a net force is applied **opposite** to the direction of motion, speed will **decrease**.

So the correct options are: **(i) remain the same, (ii) increase, (iii) decrease.**

Now **Q3** (blocks \(P\) and \(Q\) on a smooth surface): In Fig. 6.36(a), on block \(P\) there are two opposite forces **5 N** one way and **4 N** the other way, so net force is
\[
F_{\text{net}} = 5-4 = 1\,\text{N} \ (\text{toward the 5 N side})
\]
So **\(P\) experiences a net force**. In Fig. 6.36(b), block \(Q\) is moving with constant velocity on a smooth surface, so **net force on \(Q\) is 0**.

Therefore the correct statement is: **(i) P experiences a net force and Q does not experience a net force.**

