Start dividing by the smallest prime numbers \(2,3,5,7,\dots\) until you reach \(1\).

\[
1620 \div 2 = 810
\]
\[
810 \div 2 = 405
\]
(So far we used \(2\) two times \(\rightarrow 2^2\))

Now \(405\) is not even, so try \(3\):

\[
405 \div 3 = 135
\]
\[
135 \div 3 = 45
\]
\[
45 \div 3 = 15
\]
\[
15 \div 3 = 5
\]
(So we used \(3\) four times \(\rightarrow 3^4\))

Now \(5\) is already prime:

\[
5 \div 5 = 1
\]

So the prime factors are:

\[
1620 = 2 \times 2 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 3 \times 5
\]

Write using powers:

\[
\boxed{1620 = 2^2 \times 3^4 \times 5}
\]

