तुमने जो practice questions मैंने पहले दिए थे, उनके **short answers** नीचे हैं:

---

### A) Very short answers (in English)

**1) What does the title “It’s a Small World” mean?** 
It means that even though the world is very big, people and places are connected, so it feels “small”.

**2) What do you understand by “warm up” in *Tara and Friends*?** 
“Warm up” means simple activities or exercises done at the beginning to get ready.

**3) What is the meaning of “wiser” in *Little Girls Wiser than Old People*?** 
“Wiser” means more wise; a person who understands things better and makes better decisions.

**4) What is the meaning of “journey” in *Journey to the West*?** 
“Journey” means travelling from one place to another, usually for a purpose.

**5) In *Children are Going to School*, what does “going to” show?** 
Here, “are going to” shows an action happening now or very soon (they are on their way).

**6) What does “In a Class of Their Own” mean?** 
It means they are very special or unique, different from everyone else in a very good way.

---

### B) Vocabulary – simple meanings

You can write very simple meanings like this:

- **small** – not big 
- **world** – the earth, all people and places 
- **journey** – a long trip or travel 
- **west** – a direction opposite to east 
- **school** – a place where children learn 
- **own** – belonging to someone

(अगर तुमको synonyms भी चाहिए हों तो अलग से पूछना, वरना meanings ही काफी हैं।)

---

### C) Grammar

**8) Correct sentence:** 
- Children **are** going to school. ✅ 
(“Children” plural है, इसलिए “are” लगेगा, “is” नहीं.)

**9) In “I am going to read.” what does “going to” show?** 
It shows a **future plan or intention** (I plan to read soon).

**10) In “She is wiser than me.” why is “than” used?** 
“Than” is used for **comparison** (comparing her with me).

