U45: Not understanding","**Think of the decimal as a fraction.** The “8” in \(0.8\) is in the *tenths* place, so it means **8 tenths**:

\[
0.8 = \frac{8}{10}
\]

So

\[
15 \times 0.8 = 15 \times \frac{8}{10}
\]

Multiplying by \(\frac{8}{10}\) means “multiply by 8, then split into 10 equal parts”:

\[
15 \times \frac{8}{10}=\frac{15\times 8}{10}=\frac{120}{10}=12
\]

Which part is confusing: **(A)** why \(0.8=\frac{8}{10}\) or **(B)** why \(\frac{120}{10}=12\)?",Conceptual,5,5,5,10,Academic | Mock / Practice Questions | Image Upload,,,1.0000,18361,264,0.004392,"The bot consistently provided accurate, clear, and helpful explanations and practice questions throughout the session, including responding appropriately to image uploads. There were no detected failures or issues in content, context handling, or user interaction.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
