U6: MATHEMATICS-OBT-Grade 9 1. If the pair of equations ax + 7y = 15 and 8x + by = 17 has infinitely many solutions, of a/b is: 1) 7/8 2) - 7/8 3) 56/15 4) - 56/15 2. If the pair of equations 8x + 2y = 15 and 3x - 5y = 18 has a unique , what is the value of y in the solution 1) y = 0 2) y = - 1 3) y = 3/2 4) y = - 3/2 3. If the pair of equations 9x + py = 13 and 6x + 5y = 7 has a unique solution, then the value of p is: 1) p = 5 2) p = - 5 3) p ne 45/5 4. If the pair of equations 6x + 5y = 13 and 7 ^ 7 * y = 19 has a unique solution, what is the in the solution 1) x = 93/26 x = - 93/26 3) x = 4 4) x = - 4 5. If the pair of equations x + 4y = 13 and has a unique what is the the solution 3x - 2y = 8 4) x = 29/9 7x = 29/11 2) x = 29/12 3) x = 29/10 6. A shopkeeper gives books on rent for reading. She takes a fixed charge for the first two days, and an additional charge for each day thereafter. Reema paid Rs. 22 for a book kept for six days, while Ruchika paid Rs 16","I can see you have a lot of questions here. I’ll explain how to do the **first one** (the “infinitely many solutions” one). 

For the pair
\[
ax+7y=15 \quad \text{and} \quad 8x+by=17
\]
to have **infinitely many solutions**, the two equations must represent the **same line**, so the coefficients must be proportional:
\[
\frac{a}{8}=\frac{7}{b}=\frac{15}{17}.
\]
From the first two ratios,
\[
\frac{a}{8}=\frac{7}{b}\;\Rightarrow\; ab=56.
\]
We want \(\frac{a}{b}\). Use the fact that each equals \(\frac{15}{17}\):

From \(\frac{a}{8}=\frac{15}{17}\),
\[
a=\frac{120}{17}.
\]
From \(\frac{7}{b}=\frac{15}{17}\),
\[
b=\frac{7\cdot 17}{15}=\frac{119}{15}.
\]
Now
\[
\frac{a}{b}=\frac{\frac{120}{17}}{\frac{119}{15}}=\frac{120}{17}\cdot\frac{15}{119}=\frac{1800}{2023}.
\]

So **\(\frac{a}{b}=\mathbf{\frac{1800}{2023}}\)**.

Important note: this means **none of the given options** match, so either the constant \(17\) (or \(15\)) is likely a misprint in your typed question (in many standard problems it’s \(8x+by= \mathbf{?}\) chosen so \(\frac{15}{?}\) matches).

If you send a clearer photo/confirm whether it is **17** or something else, I can also do Q2 next.",Quiz_request,1,1,1,2,Academic | Mock / Practice Questions | Specific Named Resource | Image Upload | Slotfill,,Correction Ignored | Blurry / Unclear Image,0.9500,13984,489,0.003627,"The session is academic with multiple practice question requests and an image upload. The bot refused to create a full test paper and pushed a test-prep template despite the user's intent for direct help, causing unwanted template push and correction ignored issues. The bot also flagged the uploaded image as unclear, adding a modality failure.",0,full_rate,Academic,Practice / Quiz,gate_llm,gate_llm
