- **Square roots of perfect squares**: find \(\sqrt{144}, \sqrt{324}, \sqrt{729}, \sqrt{2025}\) etc.
- **Prime factorisation method** to find square roots and to **check perfect squares** (pairing equal primes).
- **Smallest number to multiply/divide** to make a number a perfect square.
- **Estimate \(\sqrt{n}\)** when \(n\) is not a perfect square (between which two whole numbers?).
- **Properties/patterns of squares**: last digit rules, number of zeroes, squares of even/odd numbers.
