### **Terms of the Subsidiary Alliance**
- An Indian ruler had to **keep British soldiers** in his kingdom for “protection.”
- The ruler had to **pay money** for these soldiers; if he couldn’t pay, he had to **give land** to the British.
- The ruler could not **make alliances** or **fight wars** with other states without British permission.
- The ruler could not **keep a strong army** of his own.
- The ruler had to accept a **British Resident** (an official) in his court.
- The ruler could not **hire Europeans** from other countries.

