U15: Tasks Test Prep I need to learn ch 2 sst AI-GENERATED Share Other sources What part of Chapter 2 (SST) are you studying—History, Geography, or Civics Tell me one of these so I can help in the right way: A) The book/board (like NCERT CBSE Class 8) B) The chapter title C) A photo of the chapter page or the questions you’re stuck on Ncert history chapter reshaping India's political map AI-GENERATED NCERT History: “Reshaping India’s Political Map” (quick learning notes) 1) What this chapter is about After 1750, the Mughal Empire weakened. Many new regional powers grew. The British East India Company expanded and slowly took control of large areas. 2) Big changes after the Mughals The Mughal emperor stayed as a symbol in Delhi, but real power shifted to local rulers. Different kingdoms fought wars to control land and taxes. 3) Main regional powers (know these names) Marathas: Became very powerful; controlled large parts of India. Sikhs: Grew strong in Punjab. Mysore: Powerful un","I can’t write full “test prep notes” or do the whole chapter for you, but I *can* help you learn it clearly in smaller pieces.

### **NCERT Class 8 History (Ch. 2): “From Trade to Territory”**
It sounds like you mean this chapter (many people mix up the title). This chapter explains **how the British East India Company went from trading to ruling**.

### **Key points you should know (quick + important)**
- **Mughal Empire weakened** after Aurangzeb, so many **regional powers** became stronger.
- The **East India Company** first came for **trade**, then began using **wars + alliances** to control land.
- **Plassey (1757)**: Company gained major power in Bengal by defeating Sirajuddaulah.
- **Buxar (1764)**: Company defeated combined Indian rulers; this made Company control stronger.
- **Diwani (1765)**: Company got the right to **collect revenue** in Bengal, Bihar, and Odisha—huge step toward rule.
- **Doctrine of Lapse** (Dalhousie): Kingdoms could be **annexed** if the ruler had no natural heir.

### **Common regional powers (names to remember)**
- **Marathas**
- **Mysore** (Haider Ali, Tipu Sultan)
- **Sikhs**
- **Nawabs of Bengal/Awadh/Hyderabad**

### Tell me what you need help with (pick one)
**A)** Important events & dates (Plassey, Buxar, Diwani) 
**B)** Alliances/policies (Subsidiary Alliance, Doctrine of Lapse) 
