Face value per share \(= ₹20\) 
Number of shares \(= 60\) 
Dividend rate \(= 9\%\)

Dividend per share:
\[
9\% \text{ of } ₹20 = \frac{9}{100}\times 20 = ₹1.8
\]

Total dividend received:
\[
60 \times ₹1.8 = ₹108
\]

