---

### (a) \(89 + 21 - 10\)

**Story:** 
Riya has 89 rupees. Her uncle gives her 21 rupees more. Then she spends 10 rupees on ice cream. 

**Expression:** \(89 + 21 - 10\) 
**Value:** 
\(89 + 21 = 110\) 
\(110 - 10 = 100\)

So she has **100 rupees** left.

---

### (b) \(5 \times 12 - 6\)

**Story:** 
A teacher buys 5 boxes of chalk. Each box has 12 chalk pieces. Later, 6 chalk pieces break and cannot be used. 

**Expression:** \(5 \times 12 - 6\) 
**Value:** 
\(5 \times 12 = 60\) 
\(60 - 6 = 54\)

So **54 chalk pieces** are left.

---

### (c) \(4 \times 9 + 2 \times 6\)

**Story:** 
In a classroom, there are 4 rows of boys with 9 boys in each row, and 2 rows of girls with 6 girls in each row. 

**Expression:** \(4 \times 9 + 2 \times 6\) 
**Value:** 
\(4 \times 9 = 36\) 
\(2 \times 6 = 12\) 
\(36 + 12 = 48\)

