U3: I didn't understand explain again","**Given angle = \(100^\circ\). The other angles are \(100^\circ,\ 80^\circ,\ 80^\circ\).** 
(I’ll explain why, step by step.)

1) **The arrows show a pair of parallel sides.** 
So the **top side \(\parallel\) bottom side**.

2) **The small tick marks show the non-parallel sides are equal.** 
That means it’s an **isosceles trapezium**, so the two angles on the **top base** are equal:
\[
\angle \text{top-left} = \angle \text{top-right}
\]
Given \(\angle \text{top-left} = 100^\circ\), so
\[
\angle \text{top-right} = 100^\circ
\]

3) Now use the rule: **Co-interior angles (same side of a transversal) are supplementary** when lines are parallel. 
Along the **left side**, the angles inside are:
\[
\angle \text{top-left} + \angle \text{bottom-left} = 180^\circ
\]
So
\[
100^\circ + \angle \text{bottom-left} = 180^\circ
\Rightarrow \angle \text{bottom-left} = 80^\circ
\]

4) Along the **right side**, same idea:
\[
\angle \text{top-right} + \angle \text{bottom-right} = 180^\circ
\]
So
\[
100^\circ + \angle \text{bottom-right} = 180^\circ
\Rightarrow \angle \text{bottom-right} = 80^\circ
\]

So the full set of angles is:
\[
\boxed{100^\circ,\ 100^\circ,\ 80^\circ,\ 80^\circ}
\]

