U6: Generate more","**I can’t “generate more” answers from this page as-is because the exact questions/text aren’t readable enough, and I don’t want to guess and teach you the wrong thing. If you type the questions (or send a clearer close-up), I’ll help step by step.**

**From what I *can* make out, this section is about Animal Tissues—especially epithelial tissue. Here’s a bit more explanation that matches that topic:**

**Animal tissues are groups of similar cells that work together for a function.** The four main types are **epithelial, connective, muscular, and nervous** tissues.

**Epithelial tissue** forms the **outer covering (skin)** and **inner linings** (mouth, gut, blood vessels). Its cells are **tightly packed** with very little space, which helps it act as a **protective barrier**. Depending on the location, epithelial tissue can also **absorb** (small intestine), **secrete** (glands), or help in **exchange** (alveoli in lungs).

**Connective tissue** “connects and supports” body parts. It has **more space between cells** and lots of **matrix** (material between cells). Examples: **bone** (hard support), **cartilage** (flexible support), **tendon** (muscle to bone), **ligament** (bone to bone), **blood** (transport).

**Muscular tissue** helps in **movement** by contracting and relaxing (skeletal, smooth, cardiac). **Nervous tissue** helps in **control and coordination** by sending signals (neurons).

**If you tell me which of these your “Generate more” refers to, I’ll expand that part:**
