U4: Political power of eu","### Political power of the EU (NCERT-style)

The **European Union (EU)** has **political power** because it acts like a **single group of countries** in many matters.

- The EU has its own **flag, currency (Euro in many countries), and common foreign and security policy**.
- It has **common institutions** like the **European Parliament** that make decisions for all member countries.
- Member countries **share some sovereignty** (they give some powers to the EU), so the EU can make laws and policies that members must follow in many areas.
- Because it represents many developed countries together, the EU has a strong voice in **world affairs**, especially in **trade, environment, and diplomacy**.

